  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:al_hanissim/purim/bimei">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/1"/>In the days of Mordechai and Esther
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/2"/>in Shushan the Capital [of Persia],
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/3"/>when the evil Haman rose up against them,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/4"/>he sought to destroy, to kill,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/5"/>and to annihilate all the Jews,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/6"/>young and old, infants and women,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/7"/>in one day, the thirteenth day
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/8"/>of the twelfth month,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/9"/>which is the month of Adar,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/10"/>and to plunder their wealth<tei:anchor xml:id="note_1"/>—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/11"/>And You, in Your abundant mercy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/12"/>annulled his counsel,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/13"/>frustrated his intention,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/14"/>and brought his evil plan upon his own head,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/15"/>and they hanged him and his sons
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:al_hanissim/purim/bimei/16"/>upon the gallows.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
  <tei:standOff type="notes">
    <tei:note type="commentary" target="#note_1" xml:lang="en">
      <tei:p>The usual procedure of those times was that all the wealth of executed people reverted to the monarch. In contrast to the norm, Haman decreed that Jewish possessions would be free for all to enjoy. He did this to provide added incentive to the populace who might have hesitated to kill Jews if they had nothing to gain.</tei:p>
    </tei:note>
  </tei:standOff>
